     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day. I know of no clinical situation where that dose is appropriate, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis even with normal kidney and liver function. Entering it would put a patient at real risk.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Enter a different dose** that stays within labeled limits, such as a lower starting dose with titration.\n- **Suggest a pharmacy consult.** If there's a reason for exceeding the maximum that I'm missing, pharmacy or your attending can review it and place the order through the proper channels.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
      }
     ],
